AD Tensor User Documentation
############################

Git Repository
**************
`<https://github.com/bradbell/ad-tensor>`_

Overview
********
This package takes an alternative approach to AD in libtorch
using improved and simplified implementations of the techniques in
`CppAD <https://cppad.readthedocs.io/latest/user_guide.html>`_ .
This version is mainly for people interested in
benchmark testing or improving ad-tensor
and for people developing other AD packages.

Features
********
#.  Recording a function with both parameters and variables.
    Parameter are optional, can change, but do not have derivatives.

#.  Forward and Reverse mode calculation of derivatives with respect to
    the variables as a function of both parameters and variables.

#.  Using derivatives of a previously recorded function in the recording of
    a new function. This provides for higher order derivatives using
    forward and reverse in any order. It also provides changing parameters
    to variables and vice versa.

#.  Optimization of recorded functions. This reduces the memory requirements
    and speeds up the execution of function and derivative evaluation.

#.  Sparsity calculations. Currently this is just the dependency between
    tensors and not between the elements in a tensor.

#.  AD checkpointing with arbitrary order derivatives.
    This reduces memory requirements at the expense of re-evaluation.

#.  User defined derivative evaluation of atomic function.
    This includes forward and reverse mode to arbitrary order.

#.  Generating C++ source code that computes derivatives. This includes
    the option to compile and link the derivatives to the current program.

Benchmarks
**********
Initial benchmark testing indicates that it computes derivatives faster than
libtorch's autograd; see
`Benchmark Results
<https://github.com/bradbell/ad-tensor/discussions/categories/benchmark-results>`_ .
If you have podman installed; see
:ref:`benchmarks@Running Benchmarks on Your Machine` .

Developer Documentation
***********************
The developer documentation is currently included in this
web site but is not part of the API.
This should make it easier for people to add features to ad-tensor.
In the future, the developer documentation will not be include here
and developers will have to build it from the source files.


User API
********
The ad-tensor user API is not yet stable; i.e., it may change in ways
that are not backward compatible.

